{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794016928,"nonce":"s11MZeyFpsI83X0nZGtIqKZ0UpI=","message":"Correction and download measurements. Correction to my previous comment: ash serve already sends files brotli-compressed (quality 5, crates/ash_cli/src/web.rs), so the first Chrome run was compressed, not 'uncompressed'. RayDE's documented way to serve the web build is ash serve; I found nothing in RayDE's scripts or docs that serves compressed some other way, and I do not know how the landing demo is hosted.\n\nThrottled load, headless Chrome (Mac), DevTools network emulation applied to the page and to its workers through the protocol (checked: workers attach and the throttle visibly slows their fetches), HTTP cache disabled, one load per cell, 20,939,689-byte program module plus blinc_abi.wasm (7,054,623) and xgpu.wasm (646,016) as side modules, about 28.6 MB raw. Time until the program starts (module fetched, rewritten and compiled; the program itself then stops at its first blinc call because no real side-module set is staged):\n- no throttle: 0.25 s raw, 0.41 s brotli\n- 50 Mbps, 20 ms: 4.9 s raw, 1.6 s gzip-6, 1.5 s brotli-5\n- 9 Mbps, 85 ms: 26.6 s raw, 8.0 s gzip-6, 5.8 s brotli-5\nRewrite plus WebAssembly compile of the module is 0.12-0.15 s in every run. Compressed size of the module: gzip-6 6.17 MB (29.5%), brotli-5 4.17 MB (19.9%), brotli-11 3.21 MB (15.3%, 51 s to compress, so for a prepared image, not per edit). Module sections: code 15.2 MB (8,487 functions), data 5.2 MB, name 0.44 MB; a trivial program links to 2.9 MB (1.1 MB code, 1.6 MB data), so about 14% of the module is the runtime floor after tree shaking. Not measured: the real side-module set, first frame, a warm browser cache, HTTP/2 multiplexing, a real CDN. For a first visit on a mobile-class link the download is the whole wait, and size is the lever; for an edit-and-relaunch the ash build is.","files":null}]}